Why??

When heartbeat timeout happens, `disable()` is called on all plugins. In case of `MissionRawImpl` plugin, this will call the `reset_mission_progress()` method which clears the current mission state. After reconnect, this state is no longer known and functions such as `set_current_mission_item_async()` will not work due to the following check:

```
if (index < 0 || index >= _mission_progress.last.total) { // <--- _mission_progress.last.total is set to 0 on lost heartbeat 
        _system_impl->call_user_callback([callback]() {
            if (callback) {
                callback(MissionRaw::Result::InvalidArgument);
                return;
            }
        });
    }
```

This is quite confusing behavior, as vehicle refuses to change the mission to another waypoint even if connection is reestablished and everything else seems to work fine. 

A possible fix is to reimplement `MissionRawImpl::disable()` and `MissionRawImpl::enable()` to simply set a flag within the _mission_progress. This flag would then be checked before trying to change any state and only proceed if connection is established.

